  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting IOM activities in Bangladesh to improve the living conditions for Rohingya peopleSupporting IOM activities in Bangladesh to improve the living conditions for Rohingya people</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2025 marks eight years since the mass displacement of the Rohingya from Myanmar, with over one million refugees still residing in Cox&apos;s Bazar-the world&apos;s largest refugee settlement. While the Government of Bangladesh (GoB) and humanitarian partners have sustained critical lifesaving support, the crisis remains protracted and increasingly complex. Through this project, IOM is addressing critical needs across the Rohingya Response in Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) and provision of Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG).</narrative>
  </description>
